1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,521
Does your washing machine smell musty, or
do

2
00:00:02,531 --> 00:00:05,398
your clean clothes come out smelling a
little bit off?

3
00:00:06,548 --> 00:00:10,019
The machine that cleans everything needs
cleaning too.

4
00:00:10,472 --> 00:00:12,726
In seven steps, you'll get rid of the

5
00:00:12,736 --> 00:00:16,244
smell, the grime and the mould, using
ingredients

6
00:00:16,254 --> 00:00:17,496
you already have.

7
00:00:17,856 --> 00:00:20,110
It's easier than you think, and I'll show

8
00:00:20,120 --> 00:00:22,441
you what to do if the smell returns.

9
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:24,163
WikiTube.

10
00:00:24,338 --> 00:00:26,787
Whatever it is, here's how.

11
00:00:27,067 --> 00:00:31,237
Washing machines collect detergent
residue, lint and

12
00:00:31,247 --> 00:00:35,347
moisture, especially around the door seal,
the detergent

13
00:00:35,357 --> 00:00:37,736
drawer and the drain filter.

14
00:00:38,399 --> 00:00:41,161
That's a perfect home for bacteria and
mould,

15
00:00:41,220 --> 00:00:43,495
and the cause of that sour smell.

16
00:00:44,157 --> 00:00:46,214
The good news is that a full clean

17
00:00:46,224 --> 00:00:49,012
takes about thirty minutes of your time,
spread

18
00:00:49,022 --> 00:00:50,762
over two quick cycles.

19
00:00:51,216 --> 00:00:53,447
The steps are the same for front loaders

20
00:00:53,457 --> 00:00:56,649
and top loaders, with a few small
differences,

21
00:00:56,777 --> 00:00:58,843
which I'll point out as we go.

22
00:00:59,400 --> 00:01:00,618
Here's what you need.

23
00:01:01,165 --> 00:01:03,706
About two cups of plain white vinegar.

24
00:01:03,998 --> 00:01:05,819
Half a cup of baking soda.

25
00:01:06,366 --> 00:01:09,502
A few microfiber cloths and an old
toothbrush

26
00:01:09,512 --> 00:01:10,591
for the corners.

27
00:01:11,045 --> 00:01:13,380
And a shallow dish or an old towel

28
00:01:13,390 --> 00:01:15,908
to catch the water when you open the
filter.

29
00:01:16,571 --> 00:01:18,788
If you have the manual for your machine,

30
00:01:18,847 --> 00:01:20,401
keep it close by.

31
00:01:20,967 --> 00:01:22,034
Step one.

32
00:01:22,488 --> 00:01:25,357
Make sure the drum is empty, with no

33
00:01:25,367 --> 00:01:28,619
laundry left inside, and check the pockets
of

34
00:01:28,629 --> 00:01:30,857
anything that has fallen to the bottom.

35
00:01:31,822 --> 00:01:34,006
Take a few seconds to remove any stray

36
00:01:34,016 --> 00:01:36,372
socks or coins from the rubber seal.

37
00:01:37,522 --> 00:01:39,184
Then take a minute to look at your

38
00:01:39,194 --> 00:01:42,537
machine's manual or the label inside the
door.

39
00:01:43,339 --> 00:01:46,475
Some brands recommend a specific cleaner,
or a

40
00:01:46,485 --> 00:01:50,257
special cleaning cycle called Tub Clean,
Drum Clean

41
00:01:50,316 --> 00:01:51,639
or Self Clean.

42
00:01:52,301 --> 00:01:54,219
If yours has one, use it as the

43
00:01:54,229 --> 00:01:55,656
main cycle later.

44
00:01:56,109 --> 00:01:58,256
Check as well that the machine is level

45
00:01:58,315 --> 00:02:00,125
and the door opens fully.

46
00:02:00,788 --> 00:02:03,448
It's a short step, but it avoids mistakes

47
00:02:03,458 --> 00:02:05,327
with your particular model.

48
00:02:05,867 --> 00:02:06,888
Step two.

49
00:02:07,435 --> 00:02:10,095
On a front loader, the rubber door seal

50
00:02:10,105 --> 00:02:11,962
is where the mould lives.

51
00:02:13,112 --> 00:02:17,035
Gently pull the rubber back and look into
the folds.

52
00:02:17,396 --> 00:02:21,226
You'll probably find dark spots, hair and
slime.

53
00:02:22,377 --> 00:02:24,480
Spray the area lightly with a mix of

54
00:02:24,490 --> 00:02:27,382
equal parts vinegar and water, or use a

55
00:02:27,392 --> 00:02:31,060
cloth dampened with it, and wipe the folds
clean.

56
00:02:32,025 --> 00:02:34,880
An old toothbrush helps in the tight
corners.

57
00:02:35,240 --> 00:02:38,017
Do this monthly, since the seal is where

58
00:02:38,027 --> 00:02:39,570
most smells begin.

59
00:02:40,535 --> 00:02:42,774
Don't use bleach together with vinegar.

60
00:02:43,228 --> 00:02:45,912
Wipe the glass, and leave a dry cloth

61
00:02:45,922 --> 00:02:47,929
in the seal to catch drips.

62
00:02:48,894 --> 00:02:51,392
For a top loader, wipe the rim and

63
00:02:51,402 --> 00:02:53,154
the underside of the lid.

64
00:02:53,700 --> 00:02:54,698
Step three.

65
00:02:54,989 --> 00:02:56,846
Pull out the detergent drawer.

66
00:02:57,509 --> 00:03:00,317
On many machines, you press a small tab

67
00:03:00,678 --> 00:03:03,800
or lift it slightly, then pull it free.

68
00:03:04,463 --> 00:03:06,761
Check your manual if it won't come out.

69
00:03:07,911 --> 00:03:09,735
Soak the drawer in a sink of warm

70
00:03:09,745 --> 00:03:12,812
water for about ten minutes, then scrub
off

71
00:03:12,822 --> 00:03:15,561
the mould and sticky residue with the
toothbrush.

72
00:03:16,224 --> 00:03:18,443
Don't forget the empty space where the
drawer

73
00:03:18,453 --> 00:03:21,586
sits, because buildup collects there too.

74
00:03:22,249 --> 00:03:24,977
Rinse the parts, dry them with a towel,

75
00:03:25,001 --> 00:03:27,612
and slide the drawer back into place.

76
00:03:28,159 --> 00:03:30,807
This one step is often the main source

77
00:03:30,817 --> 00:03:31,745
of the smell.

78
00:03:32,292 --> 00:03:34,708
If the drawer is fixed in place, simply

79
00:03:34,718 --> 00:03:36,717
scrub it where it is with a toothbrush

80
00:03:36,727 --> 00:03:37,875
and a cloth.

81
00:03:38,433 --> 00:03:39,558
Step four.

82
00:03:40,360 --> 00:03:42,846
Pour two cups of white vinegar into the

83
00:03:42,856 --> 00:03:46,317
empty drum, or into the detergent drawer's
main

84
00:03:46,327 --> 00:03:50,694
compartment, and start the hottest,
longest cycle, with

85
00:03:50,704 --> 00:03:52,410
no laundry inside.

86
00:03:53,374 --> 00:03:56,857
If you have a Tub Clean cycle, choose that
instead.

87
00:03:57,519 --> 00:04:00,226
The hot water and vinegar help dissolve
soap

88
00:04:00,236 --> 00:04:03,474
scum, hard water minerals and bacteria.

89
00:04:04,021 --> 00:04:06,321
You can pause the cycle for thirty minutes

90
00:04:06,331 --> 00:04:10,370
midway, to let the mix soak, then restart
it.

91
00:04:11,335 --> 00:04:13,960
Never combine vinegar with bleach in the
same

92
00:04:13,970 --> 00:04:17,023
load, because the fumes are harmful.

93
00:04:18,173 --> 00:04:21,226
Run them separately, and rinse in between.

94
00:04:21,888 --> 00:04:24,781
Open the door once the cycle finishes, and

95
00:04:24,791 --> 00:04:26,740
let the steam escape.

96
00:04:27,300 --> 00:04:28,472
Step five.

97
00:04:29,019 --> 00:04:32,085
Once the vinegar cycle ends, sprinkle half
a

98
00:04:32,095 --> 00:04:34,697
cup of baking soda into the drum and

99
00:04:34,707 --> 00:04:36,529
run a second hot cycle.

100
00:04:37,076 --> 00:04:39,991
Baking soda is a gentle deodorizer, and it

101
00:04:40,001 --> 00:04:42,357
neutralizes any remaining smells.

102
00:04:42,718 --> 00:04:45,378
When the cycle finishes, open the door and

103
00:04:45,388 --> 00:04:47,422
wipe the inside of the drum with a

104
00:04:47,432 --> 00:04:49,370
clean microfiber cloth.

105
00:04:49,730 --> 00:04:51,624
If you see any residue loosened from the

106
00:04:51,634 --> 00:04:53,479
sides, wipe it away.

107
00:04:54,026 --> 00:04:58,219
Some manufacturers prefer special
machine-cleaning tablets, so

108
00:04:58,229 --> 00:05:00,854
use those if the manual says so, instead

109
00:05:00,864 --> 00:05:02,779
of vinegar and baking soda.

110
00:05:03,581 --> 00:05:06,160
Check the drum for loosened buildup before
you

111
00:05:06,170 --> 00:05:07,295
close the door.

112
00:05:07,833 --> 00:05:08,912
Step six.

113
00:05:09,273 --> 00:05:11,666
Most front loaders have a small drain
filter

114
00:05:11,676 --> 00:05:13,928
behind a panel at the bottom corner.

115
00:05:14,219 --> 00:05:16,110
Unplug the machine first.

116
00:05:17,261 --> 00:05:19,190
Put a shallow dish and a towel on

117
00:05:19,200 --> 00:05:21,625
the floor, because water will come out.

118
00:05:22,427 --> 00:05:26,516
Open the panel, slowly unscrew the filter
counterclockwise

119
00:05:26,526 --> 00:05:28,208
and let the water drain.

120
00:05:29,173 --> 00:05:32,924
Remove coins, hair and lint, rinse the
filter

121
00:05:32,934 --> 00:05:36,068
under the tap, and screw it back firmly.

122
00:05:37,218 --> 00:05:39,542
Top loaders may have a lint filter or

123
00:05:39,552 --> 00:05:40,433
none at all.

124
00:05:41,096 --> 00:05:44,267
Check the manual, and if you're unsure,
leave

125
00:05:44,277 --> 00:05:46,017
this job for a technician.

126
00:05:46,680 --> 00:05:49,294
Clean this filter every three months, or
when

127
00:05:49,304 --> 00:05:51,544
the machine drains slowly.

128
00:05:52,100 --> 00:05:53,190
Step seven.

129
00:05:53,737 --> 00:05:56,676
Finish by wiping the outside, the control
panel

130
00:05:56,686 --> 00:05:58,728
and the top with a damp cloth.

131
00:05:59,089 --> 00:06:01,947
Then leave the door, and the drawer,
slightly

132
00:06:01,957 --> 00:06:04,826
open so air can dry the inside, and

133
00:06:04,836 --> 00:06:06,472
mould can't grow.

134
00:06:07,135 --> 00:06:10,768
After washing, don't leave wet clothes in
the drum.

135
00:06:11,315 --> 00:06:13,290
Use the amount of detergent shown on the

136
00:06:13,300 --> 00:06:17,583
packet, because too much creates the
residue that feeds smells.

137
00:06:18,385 --> 00:06:20,674
A quick wipe of the seal weekly and

138
00:06:20,684 --> 00:06:22,554
a full clean once a month will keep

139
00:06:22,564 --> 00:06:24,015
your machine fresh.

140
00:06:24,817 --> 00:06:26,801
Mark the date on your calendar.

141
00:06:27,348 --> 00:06:29,602
Make it a monthly habit and you won't

142
00:06:29,612 --> 00:06:31,770
need to rescue the machine again.

143
00:06:32,333 --> 00:06:35,722
If the smell comes back, look at your
habits first.

144
00:06:36,524 --> 00:06:39,449
Wet clothes left in the drum smell bad,

145
00:06:39,624 --> 00:06:42,038
and people often blame the machine.

146
00:06:42,399 --> 00:06:45,010
Check that the drain hose is not kinked,

147
00:06:45,034 --> 00:06:46,786
so water does not sit in it.

148
00:06:47,240 --> 00:06:49,587
Use only the detergent amount shown on the

149
00:06:49,597 --> 00:06:52,698
packet, then repeat the hot cleaning cycle
and

150
00:06:52,708 --> 00:06:54,728
wipe the seal more often.

151
00:06:55,267 --> 00:06:57,541
Cleaning cannot fix everything.

152
00:06:57,902 --> 00:06:59,982
If water will not drain even after you

153
00:06:59,992 --> 00:07:02,824
cleaned the filter, call a technician.

154
00:07:03,974 --> 00:07:06,066
The same goes for water leaking from the

155
00:07:06,076 --> 00:07:09,616
door or the bottom, or loud banging and
grinding.

156
00:07:10,279 --> 00:07:13,110
If you smell burning, switch the machine
off,

157
00:07:13,239 --> 00:07:16,039
unplug it, and do not use it until

158
00:07:16,049 --> 00:07:17,336
it has been checked.

159
00:07:17,900 --> 00:07:20,627
A short routine keeps the machine fresh.

160
00:07:20,988 --> 00:07:23,797
Run a hot cleaning cycle about once a
month.

161
00:07:24,158 --> 00:07:25,993
Take wet laundry out as soon as the

162
00:07:26,003 --> 00:07:28,582
cycle ends, and leave the door and drawer

163
00:07:28,592 --> 00:07:30,170
open between washes.

164
00:07:31,321 --> 00:07:33,331
Wash some loads on a hot setting when

165
00:07:33,341 --> 00:07:36,791
the care labels allow, because cool washes
alone

166
00:07:36,801 --> 00:07:38,483
let residue build up.

167
00:07:39,033 --> 00:07:41,157
Here are the mistakes to avoid.

168
00:07:41,285 --> 00:07:43,978
First, never mix bleach and vinegar.

169
00:07:44,106 --> 00:07:47,232
They create toxic fumes, so use one
product

170
00:07:47,242 --> 00:07:49,830
at a time, and rinse in between.

171
00:07:50,283 --> 00:07:53,069
Second, don't use too much detergent.

172
00:07:53,430 --> 00:07:56,287
More soap doesn't mean cleaner clothes, it
means

173
00:07:56,297 --> 00:07:58,549
more residue and more smell.

174
00:07:58,840 --> 00:08:02,659
And third, don't close the door tightly
after every wash.

175
00:08:03,020 --> 00:08:07,012
A closed, damp drum is exactly where mould
grows.

176
00:08:07,373 --> 00:08:09,360
Leave it open a little, and check the

177
00:08:09,370 --> 00:08:10,832
seal every week.

178
00:08:11,495 --> 00:08:15,035
When in doubt, follow the manufacturer's
instructions.

179
00:08:15,600 --> 00:08:16,679
Let's recap.

180
00:08:16,970 --> 00:08:19,338
Empty the drum and check the manual.

181
00:08:20,302 --> 00:08:22,484
Wipe the door seal and glass.

182
00:08:22,578 --> 00:08:24,179
Clean the detergent drawer.

183
00:08:25,329 --> 00:08:27,430
Run a hot cycle with vinegar.

184
00:08:27,976 --> 00:08:30,158
Follow with a baking soda cycle.

185
00:08:31,308 --> 00:08:35,220
Clean the drain filter safely, with the
machine unplugged.

186
00:08:35,674 --> 00:08:38,334
And wipe it down, then keep the door

187
00:08:38,344 --> 00:08:39,504
open to dry.

188
00:08:40,469 --> 00:08:44,011
Seven steps, about thirty minutes, and a
washing

189
00:08:44,021 --> 00:08:46,272
machine that smells fresh again.

190
00:08:47,237 --> 00:08:51,337
The bonus sections cover returning smells,
technicians and

191
00:08:51,347 --> 00:08:52,762
a fresh routine.

192
00:08:53,300 --> 00:08:55,957
That's how you clean a washing machine,
front

193
00:08:55,982 --> 00:08:57,176
or top load.

194
00:08:57,723 --> 00:09:00,985
If your laundry smells better, subscribe
to WikiTube,

195
00:09:01,079 --> 00:09:04,596
because we publish a new how-to every
single day.

196
00:09:04,957 --> 00:09:06,851
Tell us in the comments what you found

197
00:09:06,861 --> 00:09:08,975
in your filter, and what you would like

198
00:09:08,985 --> 00:09:10,517
us to explain next.

199
00:09:11,667 --> 00:09:12,955
See you tomorrow.

200
00:09:13,067 --> 00:09:14,262
That's WikiTube.

201
00:09:14,553 --> 00:09:16,422
Whatever it is, here's how.
